1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:06,184
Hydrochloric and sulphuric acids behave the same way, only less vigorously.

2
00:00:06,184 --> 00:00:10,937
In the cold, concentrated acid simply protonates the oxygen.

3
00:00:10,937 --> 00:00:14,479
The ether dissolves in the acid as an oxonium salt.

4
00:00:14,479 --> 00:00:18,346
This is the clearest proof that ether is a base.

5
00:00:18,346 --> 00:00:22,643
Dilute with water, and the ether separates out again.

